{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he shall not pass over him.</b> A crier's proclamation — to punish him monetarily." "<b>For every matter.</b> The lamed of לכל is superfluous." "<b>He shall be clean for his house.</b> That which is in the portion of Shofetim deals with one who betrothed a woman and not yet taken her, and went to war — he returns to his house, since he was with his brothers in war and afterward returned. That is not the measure, that he stay in his house from every matter while his brothers are in the distress of the fear of war — justice would demand that he prepare roads for those going to war and supply them water and food. But here it deals with one who betrothed a woman and taken her in marriage, that he not go out to war, and not prepare roads for them, and not supply them water and food. Therefore the verses were needed, to include his house and his vineyard like his wife."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:06.303818730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}